        rules: {
          objective: 'Score 63 points in a round and be the first team to reach a target (e.g., 500 points).',
          gameplay: 'Standard trick-taking. You must follow suit if possible, but you can ALWAYS play a trump even if you have the suit led.',
          keyRules: [
            'Follow the legal action constraints defined for 63 Pedro.',
            'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Scoring follows the game-specific point or pot rules.',
            'Winning condition: Score 63 points in a round and be the first team to reach a target (e.g., 500 points).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'If your team wins the bid, protect your Pedros! If you have a Pedro (5), try to play it when your partner is winning the trick with a high card (like the Ace or King). If the opponent wins a trick containing a Pedro, they get the 5 points, and you likely fail your bid.',
          intermediate: "The 'King Trap': Since the King is worth 30 points (nearly half the round), do not play it early. Wait until you have drained the opponents of their lower trumps or until you are certain your partner can shield you with an Ace. Conversely, if you have the Ace, lead it instantly to smoke out the opponent's King.",
          advanced: "Bidding Density: Because there are 63 points available, a bid of 40 is considered standard for a strong hand. If you bid 60+, you are effectively calling a 'Slam'. Only bid this high if you hold the King, Ace, and both Pedros. Defensively, if you see the opponents are close to their bid, sacrifice your Nine to prevent them from taking the King.",
          tips: [
            "The 'Left Pedro' (the other 5 of the same color) counts as a trump for all purposes. Treat it as a middle-tier trump card.",
            "Don't forget the 'Two'. Even though it's worth only 1 point, the team that captures the actual card 'The Deuce' earns the point, regardless of who wins the trick.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
